---
title: Beer bread
servings: 8
yield: 1%loaf
tags: [baking, bread, quick]
source: https://github.com/LiHRaM/cooklang-recipes
description: No yeast and no kneading. The beer does the work.
---

Heat the #oven{} to 190 °C. Grease a #loaf tin{} of about 20 × 10 cm with @butter{2%tbsp}.

In a #large bowl{}, stir together the @flour{3%cups}, @sugar{1/3%cup} and @salt{1%tsp}. Pour in the @beer{350%ml} and mix until no dry flour remains; the batter will be thick and a little lumpy.

Scrape it into the tin and bake for ~{55%minutes}, until the top is golden and a skewer comes out clean. Cool in the tin for ten minutes before turning out.
